error[type.method]: `.type(…)` interns into its receiver, and `N?` has no `interned`
   ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:16:1]
16 │ z.type(int)
   · ┬
   · ╰── written here
───╯
  `z.type(int)` asks the receiver to fold the type, spelled as a value, into its id
help: declare `interned` on `N?` — its seat is the enum the literal spells, its answer the id — or name a table that has one: `cx.type(…)`
